Z||000000||sloth85GT||11-06-2001||02:22 AM||||Meguiars Hot Rims wheel cleaner is BY FAR the best one I've tried yet, and easiest to use. Today my rims were gross, and I mean disgusting, it's rained the past few days here, so they were dirty with that, and also lots of brake dust, they had no shine whatsoever. They're polished aluminum by the way. Then today I went and bought some of this from Canadian Tire ($9.99 a bottle). All you have to do is spray it on your rims, let it sit for 2 minutes, then rinse it off. It works great. My rims sparkled like they were chrome afterwards. And when I went back to work (this was on my lunch break) I got a few comments about them too. So once again, Meguiars Hot Rims, if you need to clean your rims and you don't want to do too much, buy it, it kicks a$$!!!!<P>Oh by the way, if you want to see the product, click here and do some searching, it's not hard to find ---&gt; <A HREF="http://www.canadiantire.ca/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.canadiantire.ca/</A> <P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">         <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<p>[This message has been edited by sloth85GT (edited 11-06-2001).]||||reg||1
